{
  "schema_version": "1.0.0",
  "edition_id": "BSB",
  "book_code": "PSA",
  "chapter": 7,
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "PSA.7.1",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PSA.7.1",
      "verse": 1,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "A Shiggaion of David, which he sang to the LORD concerning the words of Cush, a Benjamite. O LORD my God, I take refuge in You; save me and deliver me from all my pursuers,",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.7.2",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PSA.7.2",
      "verse": 2,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "or they will shred my soul like a lion and tear me to pieces with no one to rescue me.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.7.3",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PSA.7.3",
      "verse": 3,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "O LORD my God, if I have done this, if injustice is on my hands,",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.7.4",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PSA.7.4",
      "verse": 4,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "if I have rewarded my ally with evil, if I have plundered my foe without cause,",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.7.5",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PSA.7.5",
      "verse": 5,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "then may my enemy pursue me and overtake me; may he trample me to the ground and leave my honor in the dust. Selah",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.7.6",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PSA.7.6",
      "verse": 6,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Arise, O LORD, in Your anger; rise up against the fury of my enemies. Awake, my God, and ordain judgment.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.7.7",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PSA.7.7",
      "verse": 7,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Let the assembled peoples gather around You; take Your seat over them on high.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.7.8",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PSA.7.8",
      "verse": 8,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The LORD judges the peoples; vindicate me, O LORD, according to my righteousness and integrity.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.7.9",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PSA.7.9",
      "verse": 9,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Put an end to the evil of the wicked, but establish the righteous, O righteous God who searches hearts and minds.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.7.10",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PSA.7.10",
      "verse": 10,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "My shield is with God, who saves the upright in heart.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.7.11",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PSA.7.11",
      "verse": 11,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "God is a righteous judge and a God who feels indignation each day.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.7.12",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PSA.7.12",
      "verse": 12,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "If one does not repent, God will sharpen His sword; He has bent and strung His bow.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.7.13",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PSA.7.13",
      "verse": 13,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "He has prepared His deadly weapons; He ordains His arrows with fire.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.7.14",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PSA.7.14",
      "verse": 14,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Behold, the wicked man travails with evil; he conceives trouble and births falsehood.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.7.15",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PSA.7.15",
      "verse": 15,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "He has dug a hole and hollowed it out; he has fallen into a pit of his own making.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.7.16",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PSA.7.16",
      "verse": 16,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "His trouble recoils on himself, and his violence falls on his own head.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.7.17",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PSA.7.17",
      "verse": 17,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "I will thank the LORD for His righteousness and sing praise to the name of the LORD Most High.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    }
  ]
}
